                <pb facs="1034" n="914" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg914"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2689: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-09-08T17:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 8,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 8—10:40
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>365. My 349, August 23, 5 p.m. and 350, August 24, 9 a.m.<anchor n="86"
                        xml:id="d745-f1"/> Minister for Foreign Affairs has informed me that he is
                    advised that Department of State has held recent conversations with Japanese
                    Embassy, Washington, relative to Chinese Eastern Railway. He appeared perturbed
                    that Chinese Government had not also been approached and stated that he had
                    instructed Sze to say to the Department that he expected questions affecting
                    Chinese Eastern Railway would be taken up with Chinese Government. He asked
                    whether I had any information relating these recent conversations. I replied in
                    the negative.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
